# Secrets — NEVER include in Docker images
.env
.env.*

# Python
.venv
__pycache__
*.pyc
.pytest_cache

# Git
.git
.gitattributes

# Local bot state (restored from cloud on boot)
bot.db
bot.db-*
*.db-journal

# OS / editor noise
.DS_Store
*.log
deploy_trigger.txt

# Not needed in production image
deleted_features
tests
.github
scripts
CONTRIBUTING.md
README.md

# ``CHANGELOG.md`` and ``docs/`` were on this list, and both are read **by the
# running process** — which is the one thing a file like this must not drop.
# ``keep_alive.HUB_CHANGELOG`` reads the changelog out of the directory
# ``keep_alive.py`` lives in, for the hub's "what changed" page and the console's
# Changes page, and ``utils/consent.py`` hashes ``docs/legal/sub-processors.md``
# into the revision the clickwrap gate compares against. Measured on the live
# Space rather than argued: the history page answered *0 entries, newest first* —
# a page whose whole subject is the project's own changelog, served by an image
# that did not contain it — and a document that cannot be opened makes
# ``consent.version()`` return an empty string, which makes ``consent.needs()``
# answer *no* for every session, so a gate described as being at the door by
# design was open on the only machine that serves it. This is the second time
# this file has excluded something the process reads (``assets/`` at the bottom
# is the first), which is why ``tests/test_image.py`` now derives the list from
# the code that opens these files rather than from somebody remembering.

# ``assets/`` is deliberately NOT ignored any more. It holds the fonts
# ``utils/card.py`` draws the rank and now-playing cards with, and the loader is
# written to fall back rather than raise — so an image without it produces cards
# in Pillow's bitmap font and reports nothing at all. A silent downgrade in a
# picture is exactly the class of fault this repository keeps a probe for, and the
# cheapest fix is one line here.
